<rules>
<rule id="3c67-4893-3aa1-a1e4" name="Allegiance" hidden="false">
<description>The army's Allegiance determines which characters, units, wargear, Rites of War and other options may be selected. A Legion is not inherently restricted to a particular Allegiance.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="6582-bf6d-66ef-dd70" name="Allies Matrix: Alpha Legion" hidden="false">
<description>Allies Matrix - At the Height of the Heresy. Allies and Brothers: Alpha Legion, Daemons of the Ruinstorm, Exercitus Imperialis, Mechanicum, Questoris Households, Solar Auxilia, Sons of Horus. Conditional Alliance: Blackshields (The Lost and the Damned), Death Guard, Emperor's Children, Iron Warriors, Night Lords, Thousand Sons, Word Bearers, World Eaters. Sworn Enemies: Blood Angels, Dark Angels, Imperial Fists, Iron Hands, Raven Guard, Salamanders, Space Wolves, Talons of the Emperor, Ultramarines, White Scars. Apply the chart separately to every pair of detachments in the army. An alliance never overrides army-building restrictions, allegiance requirements or the specific wording of a unit, ability or item of wargear. A Legion fielded with the other allegiance (e.g. Loyalist Sons of Horus) swaps sides: Sworn Enemies that only come from the two sides of the Heresy become allies, and all detachments of an army must share one allegiance.</description>
</rule>
</rules>
